# Y Board trace for segaybd.cpp, on top of 0001-0005: MAME's Y Board uses the
# Musashi 68000 core (m68000msh_device), so the trace lines come from
# m68kcpu.cpp: "s<cpu> INSN CYCLES PC SR D0-D7 A0-A6 SP OTHERSP" every
# ORTRACE_EVERY instructions and after each interrupt, "i<cpu> INSN CYCLES
# LEVEL" (cpu 0 maincpu, 1 subx, 2 suby), ORTRACE_PCS=PREFIX writes the
# seeds PREFIX.main/.subx/.suby at exit, ORTRACE_MSH_CYCLES dumps Musashi's
# 68000 cycle table (to check src/m68k/musashi_cycles.h). Each screen update
# logs "f UPDATE MAIN SUBX SUBY Z80CYC IDXHASH RGBHASH" (only the rows that
# update drew), ORTRACE_FBDUMP_DIR/_EVERY write the frames, ORTRACE_REPLAY
# replays tests/replays/ybd_*.rpl (P1, GENERAL, LIMITSW, DSW, COINAGE,
# ADC0-5). Build: make SUBTARGET=ybd SOURCES=src/mame/sega/segaybd.cpp
# (cpu.lua's added line lets that build find the Musashi core).

